PTX cccl-pipeline-cpasync
"libcu++ cuda::pipeline with cp.async: the producer issues cp.async, then cp.async.mbarrier.arrive (the incrementing form) and its own mbarrier.arrive; the consumer waits on the phase and reads the buffer with ld.shared (CCCL libcudacxx __memcpy_async/memcpy_completion.h:73-76, pipeline:156-189). Expected: forbidden."
{
g=5;
d=0 @cta 0;
b=mbarrier(1) @cta 0;
P0:r5=0;
P1:r0=0;
P1:r1=0;
}
 P0@cta 0,cluster 0,gpu 0          | P1@cta 0,cluster 0,gpu 0                      ;
 cp.async.ca.shared.global d, g    | mbarrier.try_wait.parity.acquire.cta r0, b, 0 ;
 cp.async.mbarrier.arrive.shared b | ld.weak.shared::cta r1, d                     ;
 mbarrier.arrive.release.cta r5, b |                                               ;
exists
(P1:r0 == 1 /\ P1:r1 != 5)
